  "content": {
    "id": "p37-q35-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "35",
    "prompt": "A tree enters a phase where it grows by $\\frac45$ of each previous year's growth.\n\nIt is initially 3 m high, what is its ultimate height? The growth during the first year is $2.4$ m.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$15\\text{ m}$",
      "worked": "The annual growth increments form a geometric series with first term $2.4$ m and common ratio $\\frac45$. Since $\\left|\\frac45\\right|<1$, the total additional growth is\n$$\\begin{aligned}G_\\infty&=\\frac{2.4}{1-\\frac45}\\\\&=12\\text{ m}.\\end{aligned}$$\nAdding the initial height gives\n$$H_\\infty=3+12=15\\text{ m}.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 25
  },
